G4314.def:
πρός, 
prep. with genitive, dative, accusative 
__I. I. C. genitive, of motion from a place, from the side of, hence metaphorically, in the interests of, Actes 27:34 (cf. Page, in l.). 
__II. II. C. dative, of local proximity, hard by, near, at: Marc 5:11, Luc 19:37, Jean 18:16 20:11, 12 Apocalypse 1:13. 
__III. C. accusative, of motion or direction towards a place or object, to, towards. 
__1. Of place, 
__(a) after verbs of motion or of speaking and other words with the idea of direction: ἔρχομαι, ἀναβαίνω, πορεύομαι, λέγω, ἐπιστολή, etc., Matthieu 3:14, Marc 6:51, Luc 11:5, Jean 2:3, Actes 9:2, al. mult.; metaphorically, of mental direction, hostile or otherwise, Luc 23:12, Jean 6:52, 2 Corinthiens 7:4, Éphésiens 6:12, Colossiens 3:13, al.; of the issue or end, Luc 14:32, Jean 11:4, al.; of purpose, Matthieu 26:12, Romains 3:26, 1 Corinthiens 6:5, al.; πρὸς τό, with inf., denoting purpose (cf. M, Pr., 218, 220; Lft., Notes, 131), Matthieu 5:28, Marc 13:22, Éphésiens 6:11, 1 Thessaloniciens 2:9, al.; 
__(b) of close proximity, at, by, with: Matthieu 3:10, Marc 11:4, Luc 4:11, Actes 3:2, al.; after εἶναι, Matthieu 13:56, Marc 6:3, Jean 1:1, al.
__2. 2. Of time, 
__(a) towards (Plat., Xen., LXX: Genèse 8:11, al.): Luc 24:29; 
__(b) for: πρὸς καιρόν, Luc 8:13, 1 Corinthiens 7:5; πρὸς ὥραν, Jean 5:35, al.; πρὸς ὀλίγον, Jacques 4:14. 
__3. Of relation 
__(a) toward, with: Romains 5:1, 2 Corinthiens 1:12, Colossiens 4:5, 1 Thessaloniciens 4:12, al.; 
__(b) with regard to: Matthieu 19:8, Marc 12:12, Romains 8:31, al.; 
__(with) pertaining to, to: Matthieu 27:4, Jean 21:22, Romains 15:17, Hébreux 2:17 5:1; 
__(d) according to: Luc 12:47, 2 Corinthiens 5:10, Galates 2:14, Éphésiens 3:4 4:14; 
__(e) in comparison with: Romains 8:18. 
__IV. In composition: towards (προσέρχομαι), to (προσάγω), against (προσκόπτω), besides (προσδαπανάω) .

G4352.def:
προσ-κυνέω, -ῶ
(κυνέω, to kiss), [in LXX chiefly for שָׁחָה hith. ;] 
to make obeisance, do reverence to, worship; 
__(a) prop. (as in cl., of the gods: Hdt., Æsch., Plat., al.), of God, Christ and supra-mundane beings: absol., Jean 4:20 12:20, Actes 8:27 24:11, Hébreux 11:21 (Westc., in l), Apocalypse 11:1; πίπτειν καὶ π., Apocalypse 5:14; with dative (of the significance of this constr. as com­pared with the usual cl., with accusative, see Abbott, JG, 78 f.; JV, 133 ff.), Jean 4:21, 23, Actes 7:43, 1 Corinthiens 14:25, Hébreux 1:6, Apocalypse 4:10 7:11 11:16 13:4, 15 14:7 16:2 19:4, 10 19:20 22:8-9; with accusative (see supr.), Matthieu 4:10, Luc 4:8 24:52 (WH, R, mg., om.), Jean 4:22, 24, Apocalypse 9:20 13:4, 8 13:12 14:9, 11 20:4; Seq. ἐπώπιον, Luc 4:7, Apocalypse 15:4; 
__(b) as in cl., of homage to human superiors (cf. MM, xxi): absol., Matthieu 20:20, Actes 10:25; with dative (see supr.), Matthieu 2:2, 8 8:2 9:18 14:33 15:25 18:26 28:9, Marc 15:19, Jean 9:38; πεσὼν., Matthieu 2:11 4:9; ἐνώπιον τ. ποδῶν, Apocalypse 3:9; with accusative, Marc 5:6 (dative T).†

G4366.def:
προσ-ρήγνυμι 
[in Aq.: Psaumes 2:9 * ;] 
to break against, dash against; 
__(a) trans. (παιδία πέτραις, FlJ, Ant., ix, 4, 6); 
__(b) intrans., with dative: Luc 6:48-49 (cf. προσπίπτω).†

G4396.def:
προφήτης, -ου, ὁ [πρόφημι, to speak forth), 
[in LXX chiefly for נָבִיא ;] 
one who acts as an interpreter or forth-teller of the Divine will (see Lft., Notes, 83f.; Tr., Syn., §vi), a prophet; 
__1. in cl. (Æsch., Hdt., Plat., al.), of the interpreters of oracles. 
__2. In NT, 
__(a) of the OT prophets: Matthieu 5:12, Marc 6:15, Luc 4:27, Jean 8:52, Romains 11:3, al.; 
__(b) of prophets in general: Matthieu 10:41 13:57 21:46, Marc 6:4, Luc 13:33, al.; 
__(with) of John the Baptist: Matthieu 21:26, Marc 6:15, Luc 1:76; 
__(d) of Christ: Matthieu 21:11, Jean 6:14, Actes 3:22, 23 7:37" (LXX) ; 
__(e) of Christian prophets in the apostolic age: Actes 15:32, 1 Corinthiens 12:28, Éphésiens 2:20, al.; 
__(f) by meton., of the writings of prophets: Luc 24:27, Actes 8:28, al.; 
__(g) of a poet: Tite 1:12 (on the use of the term in π. and Inscr., see Deiss., BS, 235f.; MM, xxii).
